<title>JAPAN: Japan chip equipment makers to boost output--paper.</title>
<headline>Japan chip equipment makers to boost output--paper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese manufacturers of semiconductor-producing equipment will boost their output to meet increasing demand from semiconductor makers in the United States and Taiwan, the Japanese business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The manufacturers include Nikon Corp, Canon Inc, Tokyo Electron Ltd and Advantest Corp, the paper said.</p>
<p>It said Nikon would expand its capacity to boost its output of steppers to 500 units a year from a current 200 units, while Canon would boost its stepper production capacity by 20 percent by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>Tokyo Electron and Advantest, meanwhile, would expand their production facilities to boost output of other types of equipment used for semiconductor production, the paper said.</p>
<p>The firms were not immediately available for comment on the report.</p>
</text>
